servings: 4 servings
---

Place a large #saucepan{} over medium heat and add @vegan butter{2%tbsp} and @vegetable oil{1%tsp}. Once the vegan butter is melted, add @onion{1}(peeled and chopped roughly). Fry for about ~{10%minutes}, stirring often until the onion is beginning to brown.

Add @garlic{2%cloves}(peeled and crushed roughly) and @bay leaves{2} and fry for a further ~{2%minutes}, stirring often.

Add @plain white flour{4%tbsp} and stir to make sure all the pieces of onion are coated. Add about @vegetable stock{3%cups} and stir well until a thick paste forms. Keep adding the stock little by little, stirring constantly.

Once all the stock is added, reduce the heat to low and cook the gravy for a further ~{5%minutes}, stirring constantly, or until the gravy has thickened to the desired consistency. Add @dark soy sauce{1%tbsp} then season to taste with @sea salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Remove from the heat, pass the gravy through a sieve and serve or keep over a very low heat, stirring occasionally to keep warm.